# power-agent Skills

This project uses the power-agent workflow system. The following skills are available as AI agent capabilities.

## When to use each skill

| Situation | Skill |
|-----------|-------|
| Starting a new feature | `feature-dev` skill — 8-phase guided development |
| Exploring requirements before coding | `discuss` skill — design exploration with spec output |
| Creating an implementation plan | `writing-plans` skill — TDD exec-plan with complete code |
| Executing an existing exec-plan | `exec-plan-runner` skill — subagent-parallel execution |
| Creating/updating documentation | `dev-docs` skill — routes to correct doc type |
| Maintaining stale docs | `dev-docs-maintain` skill — doc gardening |
| Debugging a bug or test failure | `systematic-debugging` skill — root-cause-first |
| Writing tests | `test-driven-development` skill — RED-GREEN-REFACTOR |
| Requesting code review | `requesting-code-review` skill |
| Receiving code review feedback | `receiving-code-review` skill |
| Verifying completion | `verification-before-completion` skill |
| Running independent tasks in parallel | `dispatching-parallel-agents` skill |

## Core constraints

- **No fixes without root cause analysis** — use `systematic-debugging` when encountering bugs
- **No code before spec approval** — use `discuss` skill first for complex features
- **No completion claims without evidence** — always run verification commands before declaring done
- **Repo as SSOT** — all decisions must be versioned in docs/, not left in chat history

## Skill files location

Skills are in `skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md`. Each skill contains its full workflow protocol.

## Documentation

See `docs/harness-engineering.md` for the complete system design and workflow reference.
